# Q-17: the box cancels the pending writes to the variables its block names, whichever program scheduled them; a block that names another variable cancels nothing

program cancels
12:00:05 variable:b (false -> true): block 1
  line 1 (block 1) b eq true [change]: true is true
  cancelled 1 pending
  1: variable x = false

program other-target
12:00:15 variable:c (false -> true): block 1
  line 1 (block 1) c eq true [change]: true is true
  1: variable y = false

program schedules
12:00:02 variable:a (false -> true): block 1
  line 1 (block 1) a eq true [change]: true is true
  1: variable x scheduled for 12:00:08, ended 12:00:05 by program:cancels
12:00:10 variable:a (true -> false): evaluated, no block ran
  line 1 (block 1) a eq true [change]: false is false
12:00:12 variable:a (false -> true): block 1
  line 1 (block 1) a eq true [change]: true is true
  1: variable x scheduled for 12:00:18, ran 12:00:18
12:00:18 variable:a: a delayed activity of block 1 is due, nothing is checked again
  1: variable x = true

program watch-X
12:00:05 variable:x (false -> false): block 0
  line 1 (block 1) x eq true [update]: false is false
  1: variable zzm-x-false = x-false
12:00:18 variable:x (false -> true): block 1
